Now imagine a poloidal plane. We want to show that the poloidal part of B, Bρ, is tangential to surfaces of
constant ψ. Notice first that ∇ψ is perpendicular to such surfaces, because the directional derivative along the
tangent to the surface is zero. Mathematically, if u is tangent to the surface, then at that point
∂
∂u
ψ = 0 ⇐⇒ u · ∇ψ = 0 ⇐⇒ u ⊥ ∇ψ
Since B is also perpendicular to ∇ψ, we conclude that it is co-linear to u. We have thus established that field
lines of B are surfaces where ψ ≡ ψ0.
