2.3 Step III: Using MHD stability equation
We recall that the axi-symmetry assumption implies that the toroidal derivative of the pressure is null, and
thus that the pressure gradient has no toroidal component. Mathematically, this can be written as ∇p · ϕˆ = 0.
With this assumption in mind, we now turn to the MHD equilibrium condition.
2.3.1 Intermediate calculations
Some intermediate steps are necessary before we can apply the MHD force balance in full, namely we must
define the function f and show that both p and f are functions of ψ.
Showing p = p(ψ) : From the MHD equation,
J × B = ∇p =⇒ B · ∇p = 0
